"short_summary":"An outdoor Library terrace that extends a campus work session into the open air.","evidence_claim":"Georgia Tech Library lists Crosland Terrace as an outdoor Library space and publishes access from 7 a.m. to 9 p.m. seven days a week.","source_url":"https://library.gatech.edu/about/hours","source_title":"Library Hours | Georgia Tech Library","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Current posted terrace hours are 7 a.m.-9 p.m. daily. Library access outside visitor hours may require current Georgia Tech affiliation.","cost_status":"not_applicable","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"gt-price-gilbert-grove-level","subject_type":"study_space","entity_name":"Price Gilbert Grove Level","title":"Spread Out on the Grove Level","subtitle":"Collaborative seating inside Price Gilbert Memorial Library","notes":"Choose the stair seating or a collaborative area when your work benefits from conversation, power, and room to arrange notes or devices together.","short_summary":"A flexible Library level built around reading and collaborative work areas.","evidence_claim":"Georgia Tech Library says the Grove Level contains a new-book reading room and collaborative spaces with power and data ports for study sessions.","source_url":"https://www.library.gatech.edu/study-spaces","source_title":"Collaborative & Quiet Study Spaces | Georgia Tech Library","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Located in Price Gilbert Memorial Library. Visitor access is limited to posted Library visitor hours; affiliated users should follow BuzzCard access rules.","cost_status":"not_applicable","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"gt-innovation-ideation-studio","subject_type":"study_space","entity_name":"Innovation & Ideation Studio","title":"Give the Project Room to Get Messy","subtitle":"A collaborative making space on Crosland Tower’s second floor","notes":"Bring a model, large document, or brainstorming prompt; use the rolling whiteboards and broad tables when an ordinary desk constrains the work.","short_summary":"A low-tech studio where teams can draw, build, rearrange, and think aloud.","evidence_claim":"Georgia Tech Library describes the second-floor studio as a collaborative space with large tables, rolling whiteboards, and stools for making, drawing, and building.","source_url":"https://www.library.gatech.edu/innovation-ideation","source_title":"Innovation & Ideation Studio | Georgia Tech Library","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Located on the second floor of Crosland Tower and available whenever the Library is open; Library entry restrictions still apply.","cost_status":"not_applicable","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"gt-crosland-graduate-student-community","subject_type":"study_space","entity_name":"Graduate Student Community","title":"Find the Graduate-Only Quiet Floor","subtitle":"BuzzCard-accessible study space on Crosland Tower’s sixth floor","notes":"Graduate students can bring quiet solo work here when shared floors feel too active; keep a BuzzCard ready for entry to the dedicated community space.","short_summary":"A dedicated graduate-student area for quiet work inside the Library.","evidence_claim":"Georgia Tech Library identifies the sixth-floor Graduate Student Community as a BuzzCard-accessible space for graduate students and quiet study.","source_url":"https://www.library.gatech.edu/study-spaces","source_title":"Collaborative & Quiet Study Spaces | Georgia Tech Library","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Restricted to Georgia Tech graduate students with BuzzCard access; available for quiet study whenever the Library is open.","cost_status":"not_applicable","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"gt-graduate-student-lounge","subject_type":"place","entity_name":"Graduate Student Lounge","title":"Switch from Studying to Social Time","subtitle":"A graduate lounge inside the John Lewis Student Center","notes":"Use the huddle room for a small conversation or borrow a game during staffed hours; groups larger than ten need a confirmed reservation.","short_summary":"A graduate-only lounge combining soft seating, games, a kitchenette, and a huddle room.","evidence_claim":"Georgia Tech says the lounge is for graduate students to connect and provides a huddle room, games, billiards, televisions, and a kitchenette.","source_url":"https://studentcenter.gatech.edu/graduate-student-lounge","source_title":"Graduate Student Lounge | Student and Campus Event Centers","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Staffed daily 10 a.m.-9 p.m.; active Georgia Tech graduate students have 24-hour BuzzCard access. Groups larger than ten must reserve.","cost_status":"not_applicable","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"gt-beth-cabrera-reflection-space","subject_type":"place","entity_name":"Beth Cabrera Reflection Space","title":"Protect a Quiet Pause","subtitle":"A shared reflection room in the John Lewis Student Center","notes":"Step in for prayer, meditation, or quiet reflection; leave food outside and reserve ahead if your group will include ten or more people.","short_summary":"A campus room intentionally maintained for quiet spiritual and emotional wellness.","evidence_claim":"Georgia Tech designates the room for quiet contemplation, reflection, prayer, and meditation by students, staff, and faculty.","source_url":"https://www.postoffice.studentcenter.gatech.edu/beth-cabrera-reflection-room","source_title":"Beth Cabrera Reflection Space | Student and Campus Event Centers","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Staffed daily 10 a.m.-9 p.m.; the Georgia Tech community may enter with a BuzzCard when unstaffed or locked. Groups of ten or more require reservations.","cost_status":"not_applicable","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"gt-southern-company-multicultural-lounge","subject_type":"place","entity_name":"Southern Company Multicultural Lounge","title":"Meet Around a Real Table","subtitle":"An open community lounge on the Student Center’s third floor","notes":"Bring a study group or commuter lunch and use the tables and kitchenette; return moved furniture to its original arrangement before leaving.","short_summary":"A relaxed, configurable lounge supporting study, campus programs, and community events.","evidence_claim":"Georgia Tech describes the lounge as open and reservable for the campus community, with study and event seating, a kitchenette, and audiovisual equipment.","source_url":"https://www.scpc.studentcenter.gatech.edu/multicultural-programs-lounge","source_title":"Southern Company Multicultural Lounge | Student and Campus Event Centers","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Staffed daily 10 a.m.-9 p.m. Events require advance reservation under special-use-space rules; general users must observe posted availability.","cost_status":"not_applicable","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"gt-tech-rec","subject_type":"place","entity_name":"Tech Rec","title":"Trade Screens for a Shared Game","subtitle":"Bowling and billiards on the Student Center’s first floor","notes":"Stop by for bowling or billiards and ask the desk about current availability and charges before committing; event use requires advance booking.","short_summary":"A campus recreation room with six bowling lanes, billiards, and shared seating.","evidence_claim":"Georgia Tech identifies Tech Rec as a first-floor Student Center recreation space for students and the campus community, with six bowling lanes and billiards tables.","source_url":"https://studentcenter.gatech.edu/reservable-spaces","source_title":"Reservable Spaces | Student and Campus Event Centers","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Located on the first floor of the John Lewis Student Center. Hours, lane availability, equipment access, and charges vary; confirm with Tech Rec staff.","cost_status":"unknown","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"gt-community-garden","subject_type":"place","entity_name":"Georgia Tech Community Garden","title":"Join the Campus Growing Space","subtitle":"A living classroom near Paper & Clay and the Instructional Center","notes":"Visit the garden to observe what is growing, or contact Students Organizing for Sustainability before volunteering or working in a planting area.","short_summary":"A shared campus garden for volunteering, food growing, and hands-on sustainability learning.","evidence_claim":"Georgia Tech Campus Services says the Community Garden is open to students, faculty, staff, and visitors for volunteering, food growing, and sustainable-gardening education.","source_url":"https://sustainability.campusservices.gatech.edu/","source_title":"Sustainability in Campus Services","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Located near Paper & Clay and the Instructional Center. Contact Students Organizing for Sustainability for current volunteer participation details.","cost_status":"not_applicable","under21_safe":true}],"warnings":[]}],"warnings":[]}
